&ldquo;This Ching divil comes till Ameriky to take the bread out o' dacent
      intilligent white men's mouths, and whir they try to defind their rights
      there's a dale o' fuss made about it.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Sweetness, you'd better mind your eye, now, because you beats have killed
      this cuss. You've busted his head and he'll pass in his checks before
      sun-up. You better go for a doctor, now, you bet you had.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Call those four Chinamen yonder,&rdquo; I said. &ldquo;They saw it all. I remember
      their faces perfectly. They will prove that the white men set the dog on
      me when I was not harming them.&rdquo;

&ldquo;That won't work,&rdquo; said he. &ldquo;In this country white men can testify against
      Chinamen all they want to, but Chinamen ain't allowed to testify against
      white men!&rdquo;
